{"title":"Implement fee sharing model","description":"Currently all rewards go to LPs, reducing utility value for token holders who are just getting diluted for nothing. 

Split token rewards and fees 50/50 between LPs and token holders as per Curve Finance token model - rewards can optionally be time weighted to create velocity sinks, and incentivise long term thinking.



"}

{"title":"Proposal #13: Treasury diversification proposal","description":"Short proposal description: If this proposal is accepted, 50,000 TORN-v-1 will be sold against WETH at a 20% discount, during a 14 days 1INCH limit order crowdsale to diversify the governance treasury (minimum TORN buying price is fixed at 0.008 ETH).\n\n 

TORN-v-1 is a vesting TORN token that must be transferred to governance. After TORN-v-1 being transferred into the governance contract, 1 TORN-v-1 is directly transformed into 1 TORN, giving access to the staking yield and the vote. Then, the investor will have to wait for 365 days to be able to unstake.
\n\n Full proposal description on this link: https://torn.community/t/treasury-diversification-proposal/2652"}

{"title":"Proposal #22: Governance and rewards patch after exploit","description":"This proposal seeks to patch the vulnerability which allowed the recent exploit to occur and also rebuilds infrastructure which was incapacitated by it.

Major changes:
1. Adding protection from metamorphic contracts to Governance voting process;
2. Redeploying Governance Staking proxy contract to nullify bugged rewards;
3. Return of tokens lost due to a bug in Governance Staking;
4. Redeploying Governance Staking logic contract and Relayer Registry logic contract to change the staking address to the current one.

Forum topic: https://forum.tornado.ws/t/proposal-22-patch-governance-rebuild-infrastructure/67"}

